  "answer": "The study confirmed only 1 of the 5 cases it was looking for, so the goal was not met. The confirmed case is scene 023b7fcc with the cars shifted 1.5 s earlier at 1.25x speed (S2): every run there failed, and its range sits above one half. Two of those failures are flagged as possible simulator artifacts. Triage still puts every failure at S2 on the policy: the camera view was smeared, but the car ahead stayed visible. On that scene, every setting with the cars earlier (\u22121.5 s to \u22120.5 s) at normal or higher speed failed, and every setting with the cars on time or later at changed speed passed. Most of those settings ran only once, so the pattern is a hint, not a rate. The only failure on a second scene is a single run on 09a95ffa (\u22121.5 s, 1.0x). No other scene failed in the runs it got.",
